WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.375
This guided practice reinforces the difference
between grouping and window functions The

00:00:05.388 --> 00:00:08.850
requirement is to keep every employee row but add
the department average

00:00:08.862 --> 00:00:13.150
and company average beside each employee Because we
want to preserve the

00:00:13.175 --> 00:00:17.300
detail rows GROUP BY alone is not the best fit The
first

00:00:17.325 --> 00:00:22.912
window expression uses AVG salary OVER partition by
department That calculates

00:00:22.938 --> 00:00:26.300
one departmental average but repeats it on each
employee row in that

00:00:26.312 --> 00:00:32.050
department The second window expression uses AVG
salary OVER empty parentheses

00:00:32.938 --> 00:00:36.738
That calculates the overall company average and
repeats it on every row

00:00:37.625 --> 00:00:40.825
Run the query and verify that the number of employee
rows has

00:00:40.838 --> 00:00:45.088
not been reduced Then choose a department and
confirm that everyone in

00:00:45.112 --> 00:00:49.812
that department has the same department average This
pattern is useful whenever

00:00:49.838 --> 00:00:54.225
you need both detail and context For example you
might compare a

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:58.238
patient's value with the hospital average a
product's sales with category sales

00:00:58.475 --> 00:01:03.175
or a student's score with the course average The
analytical question determines

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.425
whether you should collapse rows or enrich them
